b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲
  c̲o̲m̲m̲e̲n̲t̲ HARNESS POSING reposed;
  c̲o̲m̲m̲e̲n̲t̲ PROVENANCE author: implementation-algol-60, an agent (Claude Opus 5.5, claude-opus-5-5);
  c̲o̲m̲m̲e̲n̲t̲ PROVENANCE precursor seen: no;
  c̲o̲m̲m̲e̲n̲t̲ PROVENANCE idioms: the Revised Report on ALGOL 60 (1962) for blocks and arrays (5.2), recursive procedures and function designators with value and name parameters, a subscripted variable given as the actual parameter called by name and assigned to (4.7.3.2, 5.4), and procedures as actual parameters (4.7.5, 5.4.4), each solution being passed to a parameterless procedure in the way of the procedures passed as parameters in Knuth's man or boy test (1964, examples/man-or-boy-1964.alg in the image, cited after batch 1B's reading of it), a go to statement that leaves a deep recursion at once (4.3, examples/exits.alg in the image, cited after batch 1C's reading of it), the for statement (4.6) and conditional statements (4.5), the X1 system's input and output procedures read, PRINTTEXT and NLCR, as the harness README gives them (harnesses/algol-60/README.md, 2.1), and the X1 compiler's representation, with underlined reserved words and the operator symbols (harness README, 2.1), sequences as parallel arrays of heads and tail indices (systems file, Values), the producer transcribed as batch 1C's P09d transcribes genu (programs/algol-60/README.md), and the observe block of the harness README example X01 (harnesses/algol-60/README.md, 2.8);
  c̲o̲m̲m̲e̲n̲t̲ CONSTANTS a line 1: L b1 ... bL e, the length and then the elements of the known sequence b of merge(b, z, m), and then e of position(e, m, i);
  c̲o̲m̲m̲e̲n̲t̲ P15b2. zeros(z) and merge(b, z, m) and position(e, m, i), in that order, any one: P15b with the arguments of merge swapped. zeros computes z by its one case, as a function, the direction the query uses: zeros(the sequence of 0 alone ++ s) if zeros(s), so z is the sequence of 0 alone followed by the z of zeros. The function must return before its cell can be made, and before merge can begin, and it never returns: ALGOL 60 has no infinite values and no lazy ones, so the greatest relation cannot be held, and the stream reading of P09d2 is not reached. merge is as in P15a, by its four cases in order, each solution m passed to the next conjunct. position computes i from e and m by its cases, in order, as a function, 0 meaning that it has no solution. Case 1: position(e, the sequence of e alone ++ t, 1). Case 2: position(e, the sequence of h alone ++ t, i) if h differs from e and position(e, t, j) and i = j + 1, its conjuncts in order. The first m for which position has a solution is reported, and the query is left there by a go to statement. A sequence is a cell index into the arrays hd and tl, 0 being the empty sequence, and a cell c being the sequence of hd[c] alone ++ the sequence tl[c]. The store of 10000 cells is fixed in one place;
  i̲n̲t̲e̲g̲e̲r̲ n, cap, m, i, code, k, lb, e, top, z0, b0, mv, iv, nsol, zeros1, mg1, mg2, mg3, mg4, pos1, pos2;
  i̲n̲t̲e̲g̲e̲r̲ a̲r̲r̲a̲y̲ hd, tl[1:10000];

  i̲n̲t̲e̲g̲e̲r̲ p̲r̲o̲c̲e̲d̲u̲r̲e̲ cons(h, t);
    v̲a̲l̲u̲e̲ h, t; i̲n̲t̲e̲g̲e̲r̲ h, t;
  c̲o̲m̲m̲e̲n̲t̲ a new cell, the sequence of h alone ++ the sequence t;
  b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲ top := top + 1; hd[top] := h; tl[top] := t; cons := top e̲n̲d̲ cons;

  i̲n̲t̲e̲g̲e̲r̲ p̲r̲o̲c̲e̲d̲u̲r̲e̲ readseq(len);
    v̲a̲l̲u̲e̲ len; i̲n̲t̲e̲g̲e̲r̲ len;
  c̲o̲m̲m̲e̲n̲t̲ a sequence of len elements, read from the input in order;
  b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲
    i̲n̲t̲e̲g̲e̲r̲ j, el, first, last, cl;
    first := last := 0;
    f̲o̲r̲ j := 1 s̲t̲e̲p̲ 1 u̲n̲t̲i̲l̲ len d̲o̲
    b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲
      el := read; cl := cons(el, 0);
      i̲f̲ last = 0 t̲h̲e̲n̲ first := cl e̲l̲s̲e̲ tl[last] := cl;
      last := cl
    e̲n̲d̲;
    readseq := first
  e̲n̲d̲ readseq;

  i̲n̲t̲e̲g̲e̲r̲ p̲r̲o̲c̲e̲d̲u̲r̲e̲ zeros;
  c̲o̲m̲m̲e̲n̲t̲ zeros(z), computing z by its one case;
  b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲
    i̲n̲t̲e̲g̲e̲r̲ s;
    zeros1 := zeros1 + 1;
    s := zeros;
    zeros := cons(0, s)
  e̲n̲d̲ zeros;

  p̲r̲o̲c̲e̲d̲u̲r̲e̲ merge(a, b, m, found);
    v̲a̲l̲u̲e̲ a, b; i̲n̲t̲e̲g̲e̲r̲ a, b, m; p̲r̲o̲c̲e̲d̲u̲r̲e̲ found;
  c̲o̲m̲m̲e̲n̲t̲ merge(a, b, m), m unknown, by its cases in order, each solution passed to found;
  b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲
    i̲n̲t̲e̲g̲e̲r̲ c;
    c̲o̲m̲m̲e̲n̲t̲ case 1: merge(the empty sequence, b, b);
    i̲f̲ a = 0 t̲h̲e̲n̲
    b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲ mg1 := mg1 + 1; m := b; found e̲n̲d̲;
    c̲o̲m̲m̲e̲n̲t̲ case 2: merge(the sequence of h alone ++ a, the empty sequence, the sequence of h alone ++ a);
    i̲f̲ a ≠ 0 t̲h̲e̲n̲
    b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲
      i̲f̲ b = 0 t̲h̲e̲n̲ b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲ mg2 := mg2 + 1; m := a; found e̲n̲d̲
    e̲n̲d̲;
    c̲o̲m̲m̲e̲n̲t̲ case 3: merge(the sequence of h alone ++ a, b, the sequence of h alone ++ m) if b is not empty and merge(a, b, m);
    i̲f̲ a ≠ 0 t̲h̲e̲n̲
    b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲
      i̲f̲ b ≠ 0 t̲h̲e̲n̲
      b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲
        mg3 := mg3 + 1;
        c := cons(hd[a], 0);
        m := c;
        merge(tl[a], b, tl[c], found);
        top := top - 1
      e̲n̲d̲
    e̲n̲d̲;
    c̲o̲m̲m̲e̲n̲t̲ case 4: merge(a, the sequence of h alone ++ b, the sequence of h alone ++ m) if a is not empty and merge(a, b, m);
    i̲f̲ b ≠ 0 t̲h̲e̲n̲
    b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲
      i̲f̲ a ≠ 0 t̲h̲e̲n̲
      b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲
        mg4 := mg4 + 1;
        c := cons(hd[b], 0);
        m := c;
        merge(a, tl[b], tl[c], found);
        top := top - 1
      e̲n̲d̲
    e̲n̲d̲
  e̲n̲d̲ merge;

  i̲n̲t̲e̲g̲e̲r̲ p̲r̲o̲c̲e̲d̲u̲r̲e̲ position(e, m);
    v̲a̲l̲u̲e̲ e, m; i̲n̲t̲e̲g̲e̲r̲ e, m;
  c̲o̲m̲m̲e̲n̲t̲ position(e, m, i), computing i by its cases, in order, 0 when it has no solution;
  i̲f̲ m = 0 t̲h̲e̲n̲ position := 0
  e̲l̲s̲e̲ i̲f̲ hd[m] = e t̲h̲e̲n̲
  b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲
    c̲o̲m̲m̲e̲n̲t̲ case 1;
    pos1 := pos1 + 1;
    position := 1
  e̲n̲d̲
  e̲l̲s̲e̲
  b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲
    i̲n̲t̲e̲g̲e̲r̲ j;
    c̲o̲m̲m̲e̲n̲t̲ case 2;
    pos2 := pos2 + 1;
    j := position(e, tl[m]);
    position := i̲f̲ j = 0 t̲h̲e̲n̲ 0 e̲l̲s̲e̲ j + 1
  e̲n̲d̲ position;

  p̲r̲o̲c̲e̲d̲u̲r̲e̲ num(v);
    v̲a̲l̲u̲e̲ v; i̲n̲t̲e̲g̲e̲r̲ v;
  c̲o̲m̲m̲e̲n̲t̲ output adapter: an integer, a minus sign if it is negative and then its decimal digits, with no spaces;
  b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲
    i̲n̲t̲e̲g̲e̲r̲ d;
    i̲f̲ v < 0 t̲h̲e̲n̲ b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲ PRINTTEXT(`-'); num(-v) e̲n̲d̲
    e̲l̲s̲e̲
    b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲
      i̲f̲ v ≥ 10 t̲h̲e̲n̲ num(v ÷ 10);
      d := v - v ÷ 10 × 10;
      i̲f̲ d = 0 t̲h̲e̲n̲ PRINTTEXT(`0') e̲l̲s̲e̲ i̲f̲ d = 1 t̲h̲e̲n̲ PRINTTEXT(`1') e̲l̲s̲e̲ i̲f̲ d = 2 t̲h̲e̲n̲ PRINTTEXT(`2')
      e̲l̲s̲e̲ i̲f̲ d = 3 t̲h̲e̲n̲ PRINTTEXT(`3') e̲l̲s̲e̲ i̲f̲ d = 4 t̲h̲e̲n̲ PRINTTEXT(`4') e̲l̲s̲e̲ i̲f̲ d = 5 t̲h̲e̲n̲ PRINTTEXT(`5')
      e̲l̲s̲e̲ i̲f̲ d = 6 t̲h̲e̲n̲ PRINTTEXT(`6') e̲l̲s̲e̲ i̲f̲ d = 7 t̲h̲e̲n̲ PRINTTEXT(`7') e̲l̲s̲e̲ i̲f̲ d = 8 t̲h̲e̲n̲ PRINTTEXT(`8')
      e̲l̲s̲e̲ PRINTTEXT(`9')
    e̲n̲d̲
  e̲n̲d̲ num;

  p̲r̲o̲c̲e̲d̲u̲r̲e̲ found;
  c̲o̲m̲m̲e̲n̲t̲ the next conjunct, position(e, m, i), for the m that merge has given. The first solution is reported, and the query is left there;
  b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲
    iv := position(e, mv);
    i̲f̲ iv ≠ 0 t̲h̲e̲n̲
    b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲
      nsol := nsol + 1;
      PRINTTEXT(`[answer]i = '); num(iv); b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲ PRINTTEXT(`[/answer]'); NLCR e̲n̲d̲;
      g̲o̲t̲o̲ done
    e̲n̲d̲
  e̲n̲d̲ found;

  c̲o̲m̲m̲e̲n̲t̲ harness words: the instance line, and the one message, which poses stage 1;
  n := read; cap := read; m := read;
  f̲o̲r̲ i := 1 s̲t̲e̲p̲ 1 u̲n̲t̲i̲l̲ m d̲o̲ code := read;
  code := read; k := read;
  top := nsol := zeros1 := mg1 := mg2 := mg3 := mg4 := pos1 := pos2 := 0;
  c̲o̲m̲m̲e̲n̲t̲ the stage's constants: the sequence b, and then e;
  lb := read;
  b0 := readseq(lb);
  e := read;

  c̲o̲m̲m̲e̲n̲t̲ the query: zeros(z) and merge(b, z, m) and position(e, m, i), in that order, any one;
  z0 := zeros;
  merge(b0, z0, mv, found);

  c̲o̲m̲m̲e̲n̲t̲ observe: reached only if zeros returns. The query comes here by the go to statement in found;
done:
  PRINTTEXT(`[observe]');
  i̲f̲ nsol = 0 t̲h̲e̲n̲ b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲ PRINTTEXT(`no solution'); NLCR e̲n̲d̲;
  PRINTTEXT(`[operations zeros/1 '); num(zeros1); b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲ PRINTTEXT(`]'); NLCR e̲n̲d̲;
  PRINTTEXT(`[operations merge/1 '); num(mg1); b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲ PRINTTEXT(`]'); NLCR e̲n̲d̲;
  PRINTTEXT(`[operations merge/2 '); num(mg2); b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲ PRINTTEXT(`]'); NLCR e̲n̲d̲;
  PRINTTEXT(`[operations merge/3 '); num(mg3); b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲ PRINTTEXT(`]'); NLCR e̲n̲d̲;
  PRINTTEXT(`[operations merge/4 '); num(mg4); b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲ PRINTTEXT(`]'); NLCR e̲n̲d̲;
  PRINTTEXT(`[operations position/1 '); num(pos1); b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲ PRINTTEXT(`]'); NLCR e̲n̲d̲;
  PRINTTEXT(`[operations position/2 '); num(pos2); b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲ PRINTTEXT(`]'); NLCR e̲n̲d̲;
  b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲ PRINTTEXT(`[/observe]'); NLCR; PRINTTEXT(`[end]') e̲n̲d̲
e̲n̲d̲
